# ============================================================
# HW2 – Redis – Part A
# TASK: Ranking of the most popular products (Top-N)
# ------------------------------------------------------------
# Data type and key schema:
#
#   product:ranking:popularity   Sorted Set   productId -> popularity score
#       member = product id (p01-p15, the products from HW1 / MongoDB)
#       score  = popularity points collected from customer events
#   Product ids p01-p15 are the products from HW1 (MongoDB).
#   The ranking measures customer interest only. Stock is not part of it:
#   a sold-out product (e.g. p13 Graphic Tee in HW1) can still be popular,
#   and availability is checked in MongoDB when the Top-N is displayed.
#
# Points per event (ZINCRBY with a different increment per event type):
#   product view                +1   (weakest signal of interest)
#   product added to wishlist   +3   (customer wants the product later)
#   product added to cart       +5   (strongest signal, close to a purchase)
#
# What the task does:
#   - 15 products start with a score from the previous activity;
#   - every customer event raises the score of its product by the
#     points of the event type;
#   - the Top-N products are read directly from the Sorted Set, from the
#     highest score to the lowest;
#   - products with the same score are ordered by the product id
#     (in the reverse order for the descending ranking).
#
# Result: the Top-5 products with their scores before and after a series
# of events, the order of products with equal scores, the score and the
# rank of one product, the number of ranked products and the number of
# products above a given score. The test shows that the weights work:
# a product with few views but many cart additions overtakes products
# that were only viewed.
#
# Why Redis: the ranking is read on every page with recommendations
# ("Popular products"), so it must be fast. A Sorted Set keeps the members
# ordered by score all the time (insert and update in O(log N)), so
# reading the Top-N needs no sorting and no query over all products.
# ZINCRBY changes a score atomically, so two customers who add the same
# product at the same moment never lose a point. The ranking is kept in
# memory, and the whole task is solved with native Redis commands only.
# The ranking is used for recommendations, not for exact statistics,
# so one Sorted Set with weighted points is enough.
#
# Note: ZRANGE ... REV needs Redis 6.2+. In older versions use
# ZREVRANGE key 0 4 WITHSCORES, the result is the same.
#
# Run (redis-cli does not accept comment lines):
#   grep -v '^#' ranking.redis | grep -v '^$' | redis-cli
# ============================================================

# Clean start
DEL product:ranking:popularity


# ---------- Initial data: 15 products with scores from the previous activity ----------
# p02 and p13 have the same score (19), p03 and p15 have the same score (12).
# p13 (Graphic Tee) is sold out in HW1 but stays in the ranking on purpose,
# see the note in the header.
# Expected result: 15 (number of new members)
ZADD product:ranking:popularity 40 p09 35 p12 30 p05 26 p10 24 p01 22 p07 19 p02 19 p13 17 p14 16 p06 14 p08 12 p03 12 p15 11 p11 9 p04


# ---------- 1. Top-5 before the events ----------
# Expected result (member, score):
#   p09 40, p12 35, p05 30, p10 26, p01 24
ZRANGE product:ranking:popularity 0 4 REV WITHSCORES


# ---------- 2. Products with equal scores ----------
# Ranks 6-8 contain the tie of p02 and p13 (both 19).
# Equal scores are ordered by member, in the reverse order for REV.
# Expected result: p07 22, p13 19, p02 19
ZRANGE product:ranking:popularity 5 7 REV WITHSCORES


# ---------- 3. Customer events ----------
# Regular Jeans (p06, score 16) is not in the Top-5 yet.
# Two customers view it (+1 each).
# Expected result: 17, then 18
ZINCRBY product:ranking:popularity 1 p06
ZINCRBY product:ranking:popularity 1 p06
# One customer adds it to the wishlist (+3).
# Expected result: 21
ZINCRBY product:ranking:popularity 3 p06
# Three customers add it to the cart (+5 each).
# Expected result: 26, then 31, then 36
ZINCRBY product:ranking:popularity 5 p06
ZINCRBY product:ranking:popularity 5 p06
ZINCRBY product:ranking:popularity 5 p06

# Urban Sneaker (p09, the leader) is only viewed by three customers (+1 each).
# Expected result: 41, 42, 43
ZINCRBY product:ranking:popularity 1 p09
ZINCRBY product:ranking:popularity 1 p09
ZINCRBY product:ranking:popularity 1 p09


# ---------- 4. Top-5 after the events ----------
# p06 jumped from rank 10 to rank 2 thanks to the cart additions,
# p01 dropped out of the Top-5 (it is now on rank 6).
# Expected result (member, score):
#   p09 43, p06 36, p12 35, p05 30, p10 26
ZRANGE product:ranking:popularity 0 4 REV WITHSCORES


# ---------- 5. Checks ----------
# Score of one product
# Expected result: 36
ZSCORE product:ranking:popularity p06

# Rank of a product in the descending ranking (0 = the first place)
# Expected result: 1 (p06), 0 (p09), 5 (p01)
ZREVRANK product:ranking:popularity p06
ZREVRANK product:ranking:popularity p09
ZREVRANK product:ranking:popularity p01

# Number of ranked products
# Expected result: 15
ZCARD product:ranking:popularity

# Number of products with at least 30 points (p09, p06, p12, p05)
# Expected result: 4
ZCOUNT product:ranking:popularity 30 +inf
